      "flow": ["dispatch", "handle"],
      "notes": [{ "on": "router", "text": "spawned now, collected later", "side": "bottom" }]
    },
    {
      "title": "May this run?",
      "say": "Your `.rules` files and the approval policy decide first: run, ask, or refuse. Without an allow rule, a dangerous command never runs unasked.",
      "show": ["check"],
      "flow": ["check", { "edge": "check", "reverse": true, "packet": "NeedsApproval" }],
      "focus": ["policy"],
      "notes": [{ "on": "policy", "text": "on-request + sandbox: harmless runs", "side": "top-left" }]
    },
    {
      "title": "Ask you, only if needed",
      "say": "`ToolOrchestrator` acts on the verdict. `NeedsApproval` sends you the command and its reason, and nothing starts until you decide.",
      "show": ["run", "ask"],
      "flow": ["run", "ask", { "edge": "ask", "reverse": true, "packet": "Approved" }],
      "notes": [{ "on": "you", "text": "hooks or Guardian may answer first", "side": "right" }]
    },
    {
      "title": "Run inside a sandbox",
      "say": "The orchestrator picks the OS sandbox and spawns the shell inside it. That fence is why harmless commands may skip your approval.",
      "show": ["spawn"],
      "flow": ["spawn"],
      "focus": ["shell"],
      "notes": [{ "on": "shell", "text": "Seatbelt · bwrap+seccomp · restricted token", "side": "right" }]
    },
    {
      "title": "Output comes back",
      "say": "The handler collects output until the command exits or its yield time (10 s by default) runs out, then returns it as the tool result.",
      "show": ["output"],
      "flow": ["output", { "edge": "handle", "reverse": true, "packet": "ExecCommandToolOutput" }],
      "focus": ["exec"],
      "notes": [{ "on": "exec", "text": "still running? returns a session ID", "side": "bottom-left" }]
    },
    {
      "title": "Back to the model",
      "say": "The result lands in history as a `function_call_output`, and the loop calls the model again so it can read it and choose the next move.",
